cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EASLEE in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "EASLEE: an atmospheric Lagrangian particle dispersion model in Julia"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brioude
    given-names: Jerome
    email: jerome.brioude@univ-reunion.fr
  - family-names: Augerai
    given-names: Remi
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  EASLEE is an atmospheric Lagrangian particle dispersion model (LPDM) written
  in Julia, in the lineage of FLEXPART: forward/backward transport driven by
  ERA5/MERRA-2/GFS/AROME/Meso-NH/WRF archives, Hanna and TKE-based turbulence,
  mass-flux and CAPE convection, dry/wet deposition and radioactive decay,
  inter-trajectory mixing, aerosol optics, plume-rise and volcanic
  eruption-column physics, and adaptive/covariance output kernels — all driven
  by a single TOML configuration through one engine.  This is the transport
  distribution; the reactive-chemistry module is distributed separately.
